#{[17592186045463 #edb/ref 10 :activity.type/lesson #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045485 #edb/ref 10 :question.difficulty/easy #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045486 #edb/ref 10 :question.difficulty/hard #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045487 #edb/ref 10 :question.difficulty/moderate #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045493 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/radio #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045498 #edb/ref 10 :answer.type/math #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1003 #edb/ref 17592186046670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1003 #edb/ref 17592186046671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1007 "Multivariable Calculus" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1008 "Our multivariable course provides in-depth coverage of the calculus of vector-valued and multivariable functions, vector fields, multiple integrals, line and surface integrals, and their real-world applications. This comprehensive course will prepare students for further studies in advanced mathematics, engineering, statistics, machine learning, and other fields requiring a solid foundation in multivariable calculus." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1009 "Students enhance their understanding of vector-valued functions to include analyzing limits and continuity with vector-valued functions, applying rules of differentiation and integration, unit tangent, principal normal and binormal vectors, osculating planes, parametrization by arc length, and curvature.\nAs part of this course, students undertake a deep dive into the differential calculus of multivariable functions, including partial derivatives, tangent planes, linear approximations, the gradient vector, directional derivatives, the multivariable chain rule, and differentials. Students then generalize their understanding of derivatives of multivariable and vector-valued functions to include the total derivative of a function, second derivatives, and multivariable Taylor polynomials.\nStudents develop their knowledge of optimization techniques to include unconstrained optimization of multivariable functions and the role of Taylor polynomials and the Hessian determinant in classifying critical points. Students will also solve constrained optimization problems using the method of Lagrange multipliers.\nThis course extends students' understanding of integration to multiple integrals, including their formal construction using Riemann sums, calculating multiple integrals over various domains, and applications of multiple integrals. Students explore affine and nonlinear transformations in the plane and use this to understand the role of the Jacobian in performing changes of variables with multiple integrals, including cylindrical and spherical polar coordinates.\nThe course concludes with an exploration of vector fields, line integrals for scalar and vector-valued functions, the fundamental theorem of line integrals, circulation and flux in two-dimensional and three-dimensional vector fields, Green's theorem, surface integrals, Stokes' theorem, and the divergence theorem." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1012 54 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1013 "MVC" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046668 #edb/ref 1014 #uuid "2bbe6e2b-359a-59b0-b741-4865019fa26a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428526 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428527 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1031 "Defining Double Integrals Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1033 1990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "9cbfcac9-bcba-5bd9-9527-641435a44ebd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428524 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428525 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1031 "Double Summations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1033 1983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1034 0.549832564698138 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "c021e608-4c8b-5191-872f-f3e0b02d2d4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429149 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429150 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1031 "Upper Riemann Sums Over General Rectangular Partitions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1033 3696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "edd9f2d1-ecae-5cc2-8bee-e8544be84391" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1031 "Partitions of Intervals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1033 3697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "06d0667d-f4ac-5187-8004-79d10b9d353a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1031 "Approximating Volumes Using Upper Riemann Sums" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1033 2614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "67f29868-b7dd-582e-8c65-4c6fd95a9741" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179522 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6248" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179522 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f, P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179522 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b1f5f31f-55d0-5523-8225-03db04d35cb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179522 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})={x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179523 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6250" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179523 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f, P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179523 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7215d75e-c001-5c28-a5e7-08a74f6543d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179523 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[0,2].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=90-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(90-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179589 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9495" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179589 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [2,4] \\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 2x - y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179589 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "79b4e8e3-5cfd-5b28-ba19-f69d2c9e0c71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179589 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 2x - y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 2x - y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/de/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186567045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186567053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "db8e7d68-5731-5a44-b86e-919a13689540" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186567018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186567032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186567050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a5c07033-ef84-52e6-bd08-b1f0cc289e9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186567036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186567069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186567113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1045 "Upper Riemann Sums Over General Rectangular Partitions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186180473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0efc2539-64cd-569e-92f0-28478cfe49f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180384 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180384 #edb/ref 1061 23453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180384 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b3cd740c-76b6-54c2-b336-80c8655e0e32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180384 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180385 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180385 #edb/ref 1061 23455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180385 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7f101beb-cb03-5c90-a80d-a4c60cfcea4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180385 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180473 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180473 #edb/ref 1061 35551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180473 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0cc1df4-f684-5378-a369-66eaed4c5117" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180473 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180474 #edb/ref 1061 35552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180474 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "66e9e9d9-7c13-5958-ba9c-cefcdf240004" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180474 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180711 #edb/ref 1064 "We know how to write the upper Riemann sum for a function $f(x,y)$ over a *fixed* rectangular partition. In this lesson, we will learn how to write down an expression for the upper Riemann sum for an *arbitrary* rectangular partition. \n\nAs a concrete example, let $R = [0,1] \\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and define the function $f(x,y)$ as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = x^2+y^2.\n$$\n\nFurther, let $P$ be an arbitrary partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur goal is to find an expression for $U(f, P),$ the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition. We proceed identically to the case where $P$ was fixed.\n\nFirst, we consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{j-1}$ and $y_j$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nSince we're computing the *upper* sum, we're interested in the *maximum* value of $f$ in this subregion.\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x^2+y^2$ increases as $x$ increases on $[0,1],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x^2+y^2$ increases as $y$ increases on $[0,1].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nTherefore, the *maximum* value of $f$ in the subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value of $f$ at the *top right corner* of the subregion.\n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nSo, if $M_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ in each subregion, we have\n\n$$\nM_{ij} = f(x_{i}, y_{j}) = x_{i}^2 + y_{j}^2\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$ \n\nSince the area of $R_{ij}$ is $\\Delta x_i\\Delta y_j,$ the volume of the rectangular solid with base $R_{ij}$ and height $M_{ij}$ is\n\n$$\nM_{ij}\\Delta x_i\\Delta y_j = (x_{i}^2 + y_{j}^2)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nFinally, summing up all of our rectangular solids over the entire partition $P$, we find that the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P) = \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_{i}^2 + y_{j}^2)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j \\, .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180711 #edb/ref 1065 5800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180711 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4a36ae3f-6805-532b-857f-be7df7dceee3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180711 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343036 #edb/ref 1080 "35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343036 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343036 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5ea618ab-8cfc-5b6a-830e-0e4d5384b74d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343054 #edb/ref 1080 "35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343054 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343054 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "601a4d42-f321-5a42-9cb3-bc3cfe5f5532" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343369 #edb/ref 1080 "2{x}_{i}+3{y}_{j-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343369 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343369 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "84326603-f535-5a7d-83f9-ed0fe755c834" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343810 #edb/ref 1080 "2{x}_{i-1}+3{y}_{j-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343810 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343810 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b32ef213-5a72-5e98-8c9d-8d633f006778" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344085 #edb/ref 1080 "35-3{x}_{i}-9{y}_{j-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344085 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344085 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d2a7f258-2049-56ed-bfb5-45f8abd81c55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344515 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344515 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344515 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344515 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344515 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344515 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344515 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344515 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186343036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344515 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0a22577e-c3ef-54b7-9da9-209afaa2cf69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345079 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345079 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75339" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345079 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345079 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-5,2]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=35-3x-9y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e05635cc-2561-586f-ade2-7b1e0db5e2fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345079 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=35-3x-9y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=35-3x-9y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429149 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429149 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account multivariable: 2 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1, 2]; waits [1, 1]. Separate account estimates: multivariable=1 (2/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompa